    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span><span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip bad\">Hard</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Index as hash - cyclic sort</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/first-missing-positive/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 41</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>First Missing Positive</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">n numbers can cover at most 1..n, so the answer is in 1..n+1. That bounded range lets the array be its own hash set: swap every value v in 1..n into slot v-1, then the first slot not holding its own value is the answer. O(n) time, O(1) extra space.</p>\n"
  },
